## BRIEFS
Bipolar solvents dissolvable $\mathrm{CeO_{x}}$ nanoinks have been prepared via a solvothermal synthesis and subsequent surface modification technique. Based on the resultant highquality $\mathrm{CeO_{x}}$ nanocrystalline films, the $\mathrm{PCBM/CeO_{x}}$ bilayer electron transport layer has addressed both efficient electron extraction and good chemical shielding functions, which allows the inverted perovskite solar cells to achieve high efficiency and high stability simultaneously.
